 "explanation": "This couplet explains the direct relationship between renunciation and the cessation of suffering. The repetition of 'யாதனின்' (from whatever) and 'அதனின்' (from that) emphasizes that every single object or desire we let go of represents a specific source of pain that is eliminated. By systematically detaching ourselves from worldly things, we systematically insulate ourselves from the grief they inevitably bring. Thus, true freedom from sorrow is achieved not all at once, but progressively through gradual detachment.",
